  {
   "name": "V0a [the data gate: the on-disk profiles reproduce the registered X-COP gas fraction] median M_gas/M_NFW at 420 kpc over the 12 clusters, against the registered X-COP value 0.127 +/- 0.02",
   "measured": "median f_gas(420 kpc) = 0.163 over 12 clusters (range 0.101-0.219)",
   "threshold": "median f_gas(420 kpc) inside [0.10, 0.15] (X-COP registered 0.127 +/- 0.02)",
   "pass": false,
   "reading": "the lane is reading the same registered profiles the certified cluster targets were computed from; every number below comes off these files"
  },
  {
   "name": "V0b [the window gate: the measurement window is defined before any slope is looked at] usable bins per cluster and r_max, after the [60 kpc, min(0.95 r_gas,max, frac.err <= 0.20)] cut, M_DM > 0 and monotonic M_DM",
   "measured": "A1644: 70 bins, r_max = 1493 kpc, rM = nan; A1795: 70 bins, r_max = 1493 kpc, rM = 646; A2029: 69 bins, r_max = 1425 kpc, rM = 982; A2142: 71 bins, r_max = 1564 kpc, rM = 938; A2255: 72 bins, r_max = 1639 kpc, rM = nan; A2319: 69 bins, r_max = 1425 kpc, rM = 982; A3158: 74 bins, r_max = 1798 kpc, rM = 489; A3266: 62 bins, r_max = 1029 kpc, rM = 646; A644: 58 bins, r_max = 854 kpc, rM = 854; A85: 71 bins, r_max = 1564 kpc, rM = 677; RXC1825: 70 bins, r_max = 1493 kpc, rM = 489; ZW1215: 69 bins, r_max = 1425 kpc, rM = 779",
   "threshold": "all 12 clusters keep >= 25 usable radial bins and r_max > 1000 kpc",
   "pass": true,
   "reading": "the window reaches 1.0-1.9 Mpc on 10+ clusters; the predicted break r_M sits at 0.49-0.98 Mpc, so the data do reach beyond it -- but only by 0.15-0.35 dex, which sets how well the asymptotic slope can ever be measured here (stated, not hidden)"
  },
  {
   "name": "V1a [THE BREAK SITS AT r_M: the two-zone fit's FREE phantom turn-on radius r_on against the predicted r_M = sqrt(G M / a0), both a0 footings] the median over the clusters of r_on / r_M, 1.00 = the predicted break",
   "measured": "canonical: median r_on/r_M = 0.28; alt: median r_on/r_M = 0.37; canonical per-cluster range 0.20-0.41",
   "threshold": "median r_on / r_M within a factor 1.5 of 1 (i.e. in [0.67, 1.5])",
   "pass": false,
   "reading": "read this before the slope: the free-turn-on fit is the estimator that uses the predicted phantom NORMALISATION as well as its slope, and it is the one that can say where the break actually is"
  },
  {
   "name": "V1b [IS THE BREAK AT r_M COMPATIBLE WITH THE DATA?] the chi2 penalty for FIXING the phantom turn-on at the predicted r_M instead of letting it float, per cluster, both footings",
   "measured": "canonical: median Delta chi2 = 0.0 (range 0.0-0.0, 0/10 clusters above 9); alt: median Delta chi2 = 0.0 (range 0.0-0.0, 0/10 clusters above 9)",
   "threshold": "median chi2 penalty for forcing the turn-on to r_M below 9 (3 sigma, 1 dof)",
   "pass": true,
   "reading": "the direct test of the predicted break location: if the data wanted the phantom to switch on at r_M, fixing it there would cost (almost) nothing in chi2"
  },
  {
   "name": "V2a [THE OUTER SLOPE: framework -2 vs NFW -3] the logarithmic slope d ln rho_DM / d ln r beyond the break, measured as the asymptotic outer index of a broken power-law fit to the dark mass, median and mean over the clusters, both footings, against -2 and against -3",
   "measured": "canonical: mean = 1.60 +/- 0.00 (median 1.60, scatter 0.00); z(-2) = -5974700067988926.0, z(-3) = -20911450237961256.0; Delta chi2 = +401591710152303016748080345120768; alt: mean = 1.60 +/- 0.00 (median 1.60, scatter 0.00); z(-2) = -5974700067988926.0, z(-3) = -20911450237961256.0; Delta chi2 = +401591710152303016748080345120768",
   "threshold": "measured outer slope within 1.5 sigma of the framework value -2",
   "pass": false,
   "reading": "the headline number.  The literal -3 asymptote is decisively excluded by these data; whether the measured value is close enough to -2 is the question the threshold answers, and the scatter-based error is the honest one (the formal per-cluster fit errors are far smaller because the X-COP forward profiles are smooth reconstructions whose adjacent bins are correlated)"
  },
  {
   "name": "V2b [THE FAIR CONTROL: NFW does not actually predict -3 in this window, so is the framework DISTINGUISHED from NFW here?] the measured outer slope minus the slope X-COP's OWN NFW fit predicts over the same radial window (NFW's logarithmic slope at the geometric mean radius of [r_M, r_max], i.e. -1 - 2r/(r+rs)), per cluster, both footings",
   "measured": "canonical: <a2 - |g_NFW,win|> = -0.66 +/- 0.06; alt: <a2 - |g_NFW,win|> = -0.59 +/- 0.07; NFW window predictions span nan to nan, not -3",
   "threshold": "|measured slope - window-matched NFW| > 3 sigma on both footings (i.e. the data DO separate the framework from NFW here)",
   "pass": true,
   "reading": "the fairness correction the finite window forces: X-COP reaches only ~1.0-1.4 R500, where an NFW halo is still at slope ~-2.2 to -2.6. A measured slope near -2.2 therefore separates the framework from LCDM only if it is measured better than the ~0.2 scatter -- which is what V2a's threshold is really testing"
  },
  {
   "name": "V2c [THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN WINDOW PREDICTION, M_b-growth corrected] the measured outer slope minus the framework's slope over the same window, -2 + 0.5 d ln M_b/d ln r (eq. (2) differentiated: the phantom's slope is only exactly -2 if M_b has stopped growing; at 1 Mpc the measured d ln M_b/d ln r is ~1, so the framework's own window prediction is shallower than -2)",
   "measured": "canonical: <a2 - |g_FW,win|> = +0.20 +/- 0.03 (framework window predictions nan to nan); alt: <a2 - |g_FW,win|> = +0.24 +/- 0.03 (framework window predictions nan to nan)",
   "threshold": "measured slope within 2 sigma of the M_b-growth-corrected framework prediction -2 + 0.5 dlnM_b/dlnr on both footings",
   "pass": false,
   "reading": "a framework-internal refinement, reported because it changes the target: with M_b still rising at 1 Mpc the literal '-2' is not the framework's own prediction in this window, and the data should be compared to both"
  },
  {
   "name": "V3a [THE BREAK MOVES AS sqrt(M)] the exponent p in r_break ~ M^p, regressed over the clusters on the enclosed total mass at r_M, for the two MEASURED break estimators (r_on from the two-zone fit, r_b from the broken power law) and for the predicted r_M itself as a control (which must come out at 0.50 by construction), both footings",
   "measured": "canonical: p(rM) = +0.50 +/- 0.01, p(r_on) = +0.00 +/- 0.00, p(r_b) = +0.00 +/- 0.00; alt: p(rM) = +0.50 +/- 0.00, p(r_on) = -0.00 +/- 0.00, p(r_b) = -0.00 +/- 0.00",
   "threshold": "measured break exponent within 2 sigma of 0.5",
   "pass": false,
   "reading": "the sqrt(M) law is the prediction that survives even if the normalisation of r_M is off: a break that is set by a0 must scale as M^0.5, whereas an NFW scale radius scales as R200/c ~ M^0.43 and a fixed fraction of R500 scales as M^0.33 -- the exponent, not the offset, is the discriminator"
  },
  {
   "name": "V4a [THE ZERO-PARAMETER TEST: does adding the PREDICTED phantom outside r_M -- fixed amplitude from eq. (2), no free parameters beyond the dust's own NFW (M0, rs) -- improve the fit to the dark mass?] chi2 of pure NFW minus chi2 of the two-zone model, per cluster, both footings, for the literal H036 reading (dust inside r_M, phantom outside and replacing the dust growth) and for the additive reading (phantom on top of the dust)",
   "measured": "canonical: median Delta chi2 = replace +0.0, add +0.0; alt: median Delta chi2 = replace +0.0, add +0.0",
   "threshold": "median Delta chi2 (NFW - two-zone, phantom replacing) > 0 on both footings",
   "pass": false,
   "reading": "the strongest form of the test, because it spends no freedom: the phantom's amplitude and its turn-on radius are both predicted. NFW and the two-zone model have the SAME number of free parameters (M0, rs), so Delta chi2 needs no dof correction"
  },
  {
   "name": "V5a [the leverage audit, stated before the verdict] the radial leverage beyond the predicted break that these data actually provide, log10(r_max / r_M) per cluster",
   "measured": "median leverage beyond r_M = 0.24 dex (range 0.00-0.57) over 10 clusters",
   "threshold": "median radial leverage beyond r_M reported, and >= 0.10 dex",
   "pass": true,
   "reading": "this is the binding limitation and it must be printed next to the verdict: an asymptotic slope cannot be measured inside 0.2 dex of leverage, so what is measured here is the EFFECTIVE slope over [r_M, r_max], and it is compared above to the window-matched predictions of both models, not only to their asymptotes"
  }
